# Rover P6 3500 four-door saloon, 1968-1977.
#
# The V8 P6: the ex-Buick 3.5-litre engine in the base-unit body, with the
# 3500's grille and badge treatment. The 3500S is the same shell with a manual
# gearbox and is not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P6
#
# Dimensions 4.572 x 1.676 x 1.422 m, wheelbase 2.616 m (family figures).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is nearly side-on but not level, identified by the
# wing script and the matching photograph series. The pack covers the Series
# II car; the Series I nose is not represented. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: documented Rover finishes of the period: Arden Green, Davos White,
# Squadron Blue, Mexico Brown. Weights 25, 22, 18, 15, total 80, provisional.
#
# Speed 190 km/h. Comfort 115/503, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 115, the same P6
# cabin with the V8. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1968 intro, retires staggered 1988-1991.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p6-3500.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-p6-3500.dae. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p6-3500/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the pack is a Series II car, so the Series I nose is not
# represented; the build is derived from the P6 2200 master with the V8 grille
# and badges. The flank is estimated from a near-side view. At 128 px the P6
# body and V8 grille read as a P6 3500.


obj=citycar
name=RoverP63500(ArdenGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=25
intro_year=1968
intro_month=4
retire_year=1991
retire_month=6
speed=190
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=115
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=503

Image[E]=./images/rover-p6-3500-ardengreen_E.0.0,-33,14
